1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,460
Both engines just quit on the

2
00:00:01,470 --> 00:00:03,730
plane Gus is on, seven miles

3
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:05,290
up, and the only thing that

4
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:06,520
stops is his movie.

5
00:00:06,564 --> 00:00:08,174
It's three in the afternoon, and

6
00:00:08,184 --> 00:00:09,744
Gus is halfway through a movie.

7
00:00:09,788 --> 00:00:10,958
Then it all goes quiet and

8
00:00:10,968 --> 00:00:12,368
the screen goes black.

9
00:00:12,378 --> 00:00:13,728
His neighbor grabs his seat.

10
00:00:13,782 --> 00:00:15,142
We'll drop like a rock, yells

11
00:00:15,152 --> 00:00:16,972
Gus, but his wife just eats

12
00:00:16,982 --> 00:00:17,832
her sandwich.

13
00:00:17,886 --> 00:00:18,486
But wait.

14
00:00:18,496 --> 00:00:19,576
The plane isn't dropping.

15
00:00:19,586 --> 00:00:20,196
Why not?

16
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,640
You see, the engines never held

17
00:00:21,650 --> 00:00:22,450
the plane up.

18
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:24,260
The wings do that, and engines

19
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:25,110
only push.

20
00:00:25,164 --> 00:00:26,294
Ever coast down a hill on

21
00:00:26,304 --> 00:00:26,834
a bike?

22
00:00:27,064 --> 00:00:28,434
You stop pedaling, and you keep

23
00:00:28,444 --> 00:00:28,974
rolling.

24
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:30,288
A plane does the same.

25
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:31,738
It rolls down a hill made

26
00:00:31,748 --> 00:00:32,268
of air.

27
00:00:32,312 --> 00:00:33,702
And that hill is not steep.

28
00:00:33,952 --> 00:00:35,212
For each mile it sinks the

29
00:00:35,222 --> 00:00:37,282
plane slides fifteen miles ahead.

30
00:00:37,326 --> 00:00:38,556
That's flatter than a wheelchair

31
00:00:38,566 --> 00:00:38,926
ramp.

32
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:40,360
So from seven miles up it

33
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:42,460
glides over a hundred miles, for

34
00:00:42,470 --> 00:00:43,650
almost twenty minutes.

35
00:00:43,704 --> 00:00:44,764
A jet once ran out of

36
00:00:44,774 --> 00:00:47,014
fuel and glided seventy five miles

37
00:00:47,024 --> 00:00:48,514
to an island, and they all

38
00:00:48,524 --> 00:00:49,024
lived.

39
00:00:49,068 --> 00:00:50,688
Luckily, a little propeller drops

40
00:00:50,698 --> 00:00:52,088
from the belly and spins in

41
00:00:52,098 --> 00:00:54,028
the wind to power the controls.

42
00:00:54,082 --> 00:00:55,912
Unluckily, it's too small to run

43
00:00:55,922 --> 00:00:56,912
the movie screens.

44
00:00:56,956 --> 00:00:57,896
And here's the thing.

45
00:00:58,136 --> 00:00:59,696
On a normal flight the pilots

46
00:00:59,706 --> 00:01:01,306
pull the engines back to idle

47
00:01:01,316 --> 00:01:02,406
a hundred miles out.

48
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,010
Gus has been gliding home his

49
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:04,820
whole life.

50
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:06,090
He just never knew it till

51
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:07,330
the movie stopped.
